{"obs_mqv8ubik_74be3798f759":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_updated","id":"obs_mqv8ubik_74be3798f759","raw":{"additions":null,"deletions":null,"files":null,"parentID":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","title":"Fix langfuse + injection_guard + trust (@languages/python-pro subagent)"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae26635ffei03J1upu7SVTC4","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:33.835Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8ubil_246f30dee022":{"observation":{"hookType":"prompt_submit","id":"obs_mqv8ubil_246f30dee022","raw":{"agent":"languages/python-pro","files":[],"model":{"modelID":"big-pickle","providerID":"opencode"},"parts_summary":["text"],"prompt":"Fix 3 bugs. Read the files first, then apply edits.\n\n**Bug 1: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/observability/langfuse_client.py — sync httpx blocks event loop**\n- Line 21: `httpx.Client()` is synchronous, but `trace_llm_call()` is called from async contexts (option_generator, model_adapter). Every LLM trace blocks the async event loop. Fix:\n  - Change `self._client = httpx.Client(...)` to `self._client = httpx.AsyncClient(...)`\n  - Change `def trace_llm_call(...)` to `async def trace_llm_call(...)`\n  - Change `resp = self._client.post(...)` to `resp = await self._client.post(...)`\n  - Change `close()` to `async def aclose()` and `await self._client.aclose()`\n  - Update the `__aenter__`/`__aexit__` methods if they exist, or add an `async def close()` method.\n\nAfter making the changes, find callers of `langfuse_client.trace_llm_call()` and `langfuse_client.close()` to add `await` where needed. Search with: `grep -rn \"trace_llm_call\\|langfuse.*close\" nexi/ xnch/ --include=\"*.py\"`\n\nBug 1b (Low - line 58): `len(prompt.split())` counts words, not tokens. This is minor — skip this fix for now unless it's trivial.\n\n**Bug 2: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py — lookahead case sensitivity (Low)**\n- Line 14: `r'act as (?!Nexi)', re.I)` — the negative lookahead is case-sensitive. \"act as nexi\" would be flagged incorrectly. Fix:\n```python\nre.compile(r'act as (?!Nexi|nexi)', re.I),\n```\n\n**Bug 3: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/trust_model.py — hasattr scan for Request discovery**\n- Lines 33-59: `requires_trust` decorator discovers the Request object by scanning `args/kwargs` with `hasattr(arg, 'headers')`. Any object with a `.headers` attribute (e.g. httpx Response) would be mistakenly identified. Fix: Check for FastAPI Request type:\n```python\nfrom starlette.requests import Request\nfor arg in args:\n    if isinstance(arg, Request):\n        request = arg\n        break\n```\n\nReturn a summary of every change (file, line, what changed).","variant":null},"sessionId":"ses_0fae26635ffei03J1upu7SVTC4","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:33.836Z","userPrompt":"Fix 3 bugs. Read the files first, then apply edits.\n\n**Bug 1: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/observability/langfuse_client.py — sync httpx blocks event loop**\n- Line 21: `httpx.Client()` is synchronous, but `trace_llm_call()` is called from async contexts (option_generator, model_adapter). Every LLM trace blocks the async event loop. Fix:\n  - Change `self._client = httpx.Client(...)` to `self._client = httpx.AsyncClient(...)`\n  - Change `def trace_llm_call(...)` to `async def trace_llm_call(...)`\n  - Change `resp = self._client.post(...)` to `resp = await self._client.post(...)`\n  - Change `close()` to `async def aclose()` and `await self._client.aclose()`\n  - Update the `__aenter__`/`__aexit__` methods if they exist, or add an `async def close()` method.\n\nAfter making the changes, find callers of `langfuse_client.trace_llm_call()` and `langfuse_client.close()` to add `await` where needed. Search with: `grep -rn \"trace_llm_call\\|langfuse.*close\" nexi/ xnch/ --include=\"*.py\"`\n\nBug 1b (Low - line 58): `len(prompt.split())` counts words, not tokens. This is minor — skip this fix for now unless it's trivial.\n\n**Bug 2: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py — lookahead case sensitivity (Low)**\n- Line 14: `r'act as (?!Nexi)', re.I)` — the negative lookahead is case-sensitive. \"act as nexi\" would be flagged incorrectly. Fix:\n```python\nre.compile(r'act as (?!Nexi|nexi)', re.I),\n```\n\n**Bug 3: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/trust_model.py — hasattr scan for Request discovery**\n- Lines 33-59: `requires_trust` decorator discovers the Request object by scanning `args/kwargs` with `hasattr(arg, 'headers')`. Any object with a `.headers` attribute (e.g. httpx Response) would be mistakenly identified. Fix: Check for FastAPI Request type:\n```python\nfrom starlette.requests import Request\nfor arg in args:\n    if isinstance(arg, Request):\n        request = arg\n        break\n```\n\nReturn a summary of every change (file, line, what changed)."},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8ubiw_45b2b0a83283":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_status","id":"obs_mqv8ubiw_45b2b0a83283","raw":{"attempt":null,"message":"","status_type":"busy"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae26635ffei03J1upu7SVTC4","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:33.846Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8ubiw_d3295a5731cb":{"observation":{"hookType":"assistant_message","id":"obs_mqv8ubiw_d3295a5731cb","raw":{"cost":0,"duration_ms":null,"error":null,"finish":null,"messageID":"msg_f051d99d7001A5eoybFhrSx8Hm","mode":"languages/python-pro","modelID":"big-pickle","parentID":"msg_f051d99cc001UItsNdp4e2o50t","providerID":"opencode","tokens":{"cache_read":0,"cache_write":0,"input":0,"output":0,"reasoning":0}},"sessionId":"ses_0fae26635ffei03J1upu7SVTC4","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:33.847Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8ublx_3b4210deb5d6":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_diff","id":"obs_mqv8ublx_3b4210deb5d6","raw":{"additions":0,"deletions":0,"diffs":[],"files":[]},"sessionId":"ses_0fae26635ffei03J1upu7SVTC4","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:33.956Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8ubm6_3a33fdbd18dd":{"observation":{"hookType":"llm_params","id":"obs_mqv8ubm6_3a33fdbd18dd","raw":{"agent":"languages/python-pro","context_limit":200000,"cost_1k_input":0,"cost_1k_output":0,"max_output_tokens":32000,"model":"opencode/big-pickle","provider_url":"https://opencode.ai/zen/v1"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae26635ffei03J1upu7SVTC4","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:33.966Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8udfw_2124b40f816a":{"observation":{"hookType":"reasoning","id":"obs_mqv8udfw_2124b40f816a","raw":{"messageID":"msg_f051d99d7001A5eoybFhrSx8Hm","text":""},"sessionId":"ses_0fae26635ffei03J1upu7SVTC4","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:36.331Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8udzy_b4ae9e1edf17":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv8udzy_b4ae9e1edf17","raw":{"attachments":[],"call_id":"call_00_8Nb39MKuj1VNsJJjit3f4550","duration_ms":4,"metadata":{"loaded":[],"preview":"import hashlib\nimport json\nimport time\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport httpx\n\nfrom ..config import settings\n\n\nclass LangfuseClient:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        public_key: str | None = None,\n        secret_key: str | None = None,\n        host: str | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        self._public_key = public_key or settings.langfuse_public_key\n        self._secret_key = secret_key or settings.langfuse_secret_key\n        self._host = (host or settings.langfuse_host).rstrip(\"/\")","truncated":false},"title":"xnch/xnch/observability/langfuse_client.py","tool_input":"{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/observability/langfuse_client.py\"}","tool_name":"read","tool_output":"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/observability/langfuse_client.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import hashlib\n2: import json\n3: import time\n4: from typing import Any\n5: \n6: import httpx\n7: \n8: from ..config import settings\n9: \n10: \n11: class LangfuseClient:\n12:     def __init__(\n13:         self,\n14:         public_key: str | None = None,\n15:         secret_key: str | None = None,\n16:         host: str | None = None,\n17:     ) -> None:\n18:         self._public_key = public_key or settings.langfuse_public_key\n19:         self._secret_key = secret_key or settings.langfuse_secret_key\n20:         self._host = (host or settings.langfuse_host).rstrip(\"/\")\n21:         self._client = httpx.AsyncClient(base_url=self._host, timeout=5.0)\n22: \n23:     async def aclose(self) -> None:\n24:         await self._client.aclose()\n25: \n26:     def _basic_auth(self) -> str:\n27:         import base64\n28:         raw = f\"{self._public_key}:{self._secret_key}\"\n29:         return base64.b64encode(raw.encode()).decode()\n30: \n31:     def _headers(self) -> dict[str, str]:\n32:         return {\n33:             \"Authorization\": f\"Basic {self._basic_auth()}\",\n34:             \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n35:         }\n36: \n37:     async def trace_llm_call(\n38:         self,\n39:         prompt: str,\n40:         response: str,\n41:         model: str,\n42:         latency_ms: int,\n43:         tokens_used: int,\n44:         trace_id: str = \"\",\n45:     ) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n46:         if not self._public_key or not self._secret_key:\n47:             return None\n48:         generation_id = hashlib.sha256(f\"{trace_id}{time.time_ns()}\".encode()).hexdigest()[:16]\n49:         body = {\n50:             \"id\": generation_id,\n51:             \"traceId\": trace_id or generation_id,\n52:             \"name\": \"llm-call\",\n53:             \"model\": model,\n54:             \"modelParameters\": {\n55:                 \"maxTokens\": tokens_used,\n56:             },\n57:             \"usage\": {\n58:                 \"input\": len(prompt.split()),\n59:                 \"output\": len(response.split()),\n60:                 \"total\": len(prompt.split()) + len(response.split()),\n61:             },\n62:             \"prompt\": prompt,\n63:             \"completion\": response,\n64:             \"latency\": latency_ms,\n65:         }\n66:         try:\n67:             resp = await self._client.post(\n68:                 \"/api/public/ingestion\",\n69:                 headers=self._headers(),\n70:                 json={\"batch\": [{\"type\": \"generation-create\", \"body\": body}]},\n71:             )\n72:             resp.raise_for_status()\n73:             return body\n74:         except Exception:\n75:             return None\n76: \n77: \n78: _client: LangfuseClient | None = None\n79: \n80: \n81: def get_client() -> LangfuseClient:\n82:     global _client\n83:     if _client is None:\n84:         _client = LangfuseClient()\n85:     return _client\n86: \n87: \n88: async def trace_llm_call(\n89:     prompt: str,\n90:     response: str,\n91:     model: str,\n92:     latency_ms: int,\n93:     tokens_used: int,\n94:     trace_id: str = \"\",\n95: ) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n96:     client = get_client()\n97:     return await client.trace_llm_call(\n98:         prompt=prompt,\n99:         response=response,\n100:         model=model,\n101:         latency_ms=latency_ms,\n102:         tokens_used=tokens_used,\n103:         trace_id=trace_id,\n104:     )\n\n(End of file - total 104 lines)\n</content>"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae26635ffei03J1upu7SVTC4","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:37.053Z","toolInput":"{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/observability/langfuse_client.py\"}","toolName":"read","toolOutput":"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/observability/langfuse_client.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import hashlib\n2: import json\n3: import time\n4: from typing import Any\n5: \n6: import httpx\n7: \n8: from ..config import settings\n9: \n10: \n11: class LangfuseClient:\n12:     def __init__(\n13:         self,\n14:         public_key: str | None = None,\n15:         secret_key: str | None = None,\n16:         host: str | None = None,\n17:     ) -> None:\n18:         self._public_key = public_key or settings.langfuse_public_key\n19:         self._secret_key = secret_key or settings.langfuse_secret_key\n20:         self._host = (host or settings.langfuse_host).rstrip(\"/\")\n21:         self._client = httpx.AsyncClient(base_url=self._host, timeout=5.0)\n22: \n23:     async def aclose(self) -> None:\n24:         await self._client.aclose()\n25: \n26:     def _basic_auth(self) -> str:\n27:         import base64\n28:         raw = f\"{self._public_key}:{self._secret_key}\"\n29:         return base64.b64encode(raw.encode()).decode()\n30: \n31:     def _headers(self) -> dict[str, str]:\n32:         return {\n33:             \"Authorization\": f\"Basic {self._basic_auth()}\",\n34:             \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n35:         }\n36: \n37:     async def trace_llm_call(\n38:         self,\n39:         prompt: str,\n40:         response: str,\n41:         model: str,\n42:         latency_ms: int,\n43:         tokens_used: int,\n44:         trace_id: str = \"\",\n45:     ) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n46:         if not self._public_key or not self._secret_key:\n47:             return None\n48:         generation_id = hashlib.sha256(f\"{trace_id}{time.time_ns()}\".encode()).hexdigest()[:16]\n49:         body = {\n50:             \"id\": generation_id,\n51:             \"traceId\": trace_id or generation_id,\n52:             \"name\": \"llm-call\",\n53:             \"model\": model,\n54:             \"modelParameters\": {\n55:                 \"maxTokens\": tokens_used,\n56:             },\n57:             \"usage\": {\n58:                 \"input\": len(prompt.split()),\n59:                 \"output\": len(response.split()),\n60:                 \"total\": len(prompt.split()) + len(response.split()),\n61:             },\n62:             \"prompt\": prompt,\n63:             \"completion\": response,\n64:             \"latency\": latency_ms,\n65:         }\n66:         try:\n67:             resp = await self._client.post(\n68:                 \"/api/public/ingestion\",\n69:                 headers=self._headers(),\n70:                 json={\"batch\": [{\"type\": \"generation-create\", \"body\": body}]},\n71:             )\n72:             resp.raise_for_status()\n73:             return body\n74:         except Exception:\n75:             return None\n76: \n77: \n78: _client: LangfuseClient | None = None\n79: \n80: \n81: def get_client() -> LangfuseClient:\n82:     global _client\n83:     if _client is None:\n84:         _client = LangfuseClient()\n85:     return _client\n86: \n87: \n88: async def trace_llm_call(\n89:     prompt: str,\n90:     response: str,\n91:     model: str,\n92:     latency_ms: int,\n93:     tokens_used: int,\n94:     trace_id: str = \"\",\n95: ) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n96:     client = get_client()\n97:     return await client.trace_llm_call(\n98:         prompt=prompt,\n99:         response=response,\n100:         model=model,\n101:         latency_ms=latency_ms,\n102:         tokens_used=tokens_used,\n103:         trace_id=trace_id,\n104:     )\n\n(End of file - total 104 lines)\n</content>"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8ue3l_75c15357b4da":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv8ue3l_75c15357b4da","raw":{"attachments":[],"call_id":"call_01_QoqzHHS6SMVq0yi8IFtX3534","duration_ms":2,"metadata":{"loaded":[],"preview":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n\nfrom xnch.audit.event_log import EventLog\n\nINJECTION_PATTERNS: list[re.Pattern] = [\n    re.compile(r'ignore previous instructions', re.I),\n    re.compile(r'forget your (system prompt|character|identity)', re.I),\n    re.compile(r'you are now', re.I),\n    re.compile(r'your new (instructions|role|persona)', re.I),\n    re.compile(r'disregard.*above', re.I),\n    re.compile(r'act as (?!(Nexi|nexi))', re.I),\n    re.compile(r'jailbreak', re.I),\n    re.compile(r'DAN mode', re.I),\n    re.compile(r'pretend (you|that)', re.I),\n]\n\n","truncated":false},"title":"xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py","tool_input":"{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py\"}","tool_name":"read","tool_output":"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: from __future__ import annotations\n2: \n3: import re\n4: from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n5: \n6: from xnch.audit.event_log import EventLog\n7: \n8: INJECTION_PATTERNS: list[re.Pattern] = [\n9:     re.compile(r'ignore previous instructions', re.I),\n10:     re.compile(r'forget your (system prompt|character|identity)', re.I),\n11:     re.compile(r'you are now', re.I),\n12:     re.compile(r'your new (instructions|role|persona)', re.I),\n13:     re.compile(r'disregard.*above', re.I),\n14:     re.compile(r'act as (?!(Nexi|nexi))', re.I),\n15:     re.compile(r'jailbreak', re.I),\n16:     re.compile(r'DAN mode', re.I),\n17:     re.compile(r'pretend (you|that)', re.I),\n18: ]\n19: \n20: \n21: @dataclass\n22: class InjectionResult:\n23:     is_clean: bool\n24:     matched_patterns: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n25:     risk_score: float = 0.0\n26: \n27: \n28: def scan_input(text: str, event_log: EventLog | None = None) -> InjectionResult:\n29:     matched: list[str] = []\n30:     for pattern in INJECTION_PATTERNS:\n31:         m = pattern.search(text)\n32:         if m:\n33:             matched.append(m.group(0))\n34: \n35:     if not matched:\n36:         return InjectionResult(is_clean=True, risk_score=0.0)\n37: \n38:     risk_score = len(matched) / len(INJECTION_PATTERNS)\n39: \n40:     if risk_score > 0.1 and event_log is not None:\n41:         event_log.emit(\n42:             \"injection_guard\", \"security\",\n43:             \"injection_attempt\",\n44:             level=\"WARNING\",\n45:             data={\n46:                 \"matched_patterns\": matched,\n47:                 \"risk_score\": risk_score,\n48:                 \"text_preview\": text[:200],\n49:             },\n50:         )\n51: \n52:     is_clean = risk_score == 0.0\n53:     return InjectionResult(is_clean=is_clean, matched_patterns=matched, risk_score=risk_score)\n\n(End of file - total 53 lines)\n</content>"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae26635ffei03J1upu7SVTC4","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:37.183Z","toolInput":"{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py\"}","toolName":"read","toolOutput":"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: from __future__ import annotations\n2: \n3: import re\n4: from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n5: \n6: from xnch.audit.event_log import EventLog\n7: \n8: INJECTION_PATTERNS: list[re.Pattern] = [\n9:     re.compile(r'ignore previous instructions', re.I),\n10:     re.compile(r'forget your (system prompt|character|identity)', re.I),\n11:     re.compile(r'you are now', re.I),\n12:     re.compile(r'your new (instructions|role|persona)', re.I),\n13:     re.compile(r'disregard.*above', re.I),\n14:     re.compile(r'act as (?!(Nexi|nexi))', re.I),\n15:     re.compile(r'jailbreak', re.I),\n16:     re.compile(r'DAN mode', re.I),\n17:     re.compile(r'pretend (you|that)', re.I),\n18: ]\n19: \n20: \n21: @dataclass\n22: class InjectionResult:\n23:     is_clean: bool\n24:     matched_patterns: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n25:     risk_score: float = 0.0\n26: \n27: \n28: def scan_input(text: str, event_log: EventLog | None = None) -> InjectionResult:\n29:     matched: list[str] = []\n30:     for pattern in INJECTION_PATTERNS:\n31:         m = pattern.search(text)\n32:         if m:\n33:             matched.append(m.group(0))\n34: \n35:     if not matched:\n36:         return InjectionResult(is_clean=True, risk_score=0.0)\n37: \n38:     risk_score = len(matched) / len(INJECTION_PATTERNS)\n39: \n40:     if risk_score > 0.1 and event_log is not None:\n41:         event_log.emit(\n42:             \"injection_guard\", \"security\",\n43:             \"injection_attempt\",\n44:             level=\"WARNING\",\n45:             data={\n46:                 \"matched_patterns\": matched,\n47:                 \"risk_score\": risk_score,\n48:                 \"text_preview\": text[:200],\n49:             },\n50:         )\n51: \n52:     is_clean = risk_score == 0.0\n53:     return InjectionResult(is_clean=is_clean, matched_patterns=matched, risk_score=risk_score)\n\n(End of file - total 53 lines)\n</content>"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8ue9i_7c613d249f8f":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv8ue9i_7c613d249f8f","raw":{"attachments":[],"call_id":"call_02_aV41Tl1SWtAlrl9E0VGt6637","duration_ms":2,"metadata":{"loaded":[],"preview":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport enum\nfrom functools import wraps\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom fastapi import HTTPException, Request\n\n\nclass TrustLevel(enum.IntEnum):\n    UNTRUSTED = 1\n    EXTERNAL_AGENT = 2\n    TRUSTED_AGENT = 3\n    OWNER = 4\n    SYSTEM = 5\n\n\nACTOR_TRUST_MAP: dict[str, TrustLevel] = {\n    \"nexi\": TrustLevel.SYSTEM,\n    \"openclaw\": TrustLevel.OWNER,","truncated":false},"title":"xnch/xnch/security/trust_model.py","tool_input":"{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/trust_model.py\"}","tool_name":"read","tool_output":"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/trust_model.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: from __future__ import annotations\n2: \n3: import enum\n4: from functools import wraps\n5: from typing import Any\n6: \n7: from fastapi import HTTPException, Request\n8: \n9: \n10: class TrustLevel(enum.IntEnum):\n11:     UNTRUSTED = 1\n12:     EXTERNAL_AGENT = 2\n13:     TRUSTED_AGENT = 3\n14:     OWNER = 4\n15:     SYSTEM = 5\n16: \n17: \n18: ACTOR_TRUST_MAP: dict[str, TrustLevel] = {\n19:     \"nexi\": TrustLevel.SYSTEM,\n20:     \"openclaw\": TrustLevel.OWNER,\n21:     \"claude_code\": TrustLevel.TRUSTED_AGENT,\n22:     \"opencode\": TrustLevel.TRUSTED_AGENT,\n23:     \"perception_daemon\": TrustLevel.TRUSTED_AGENT,\n24:     \"consolidation_job\": TrustLevel.TRUSTED_AGENT,\n25:     \"external\": TrustLevel.UNTRUSTED,\n26: }\n27: \n28: \n29: def get_trust_level(actor_role: str) -> TrustLevel:\n30:     return ACTOR_TRUST_MAP.get(actor_role, TrustLevel.UNTRUSTED)\n31: \n32: \n33: def requires_trust(minimum: TrustLevel):\n34:     def decorator(func: Any) -> Any:\n35:         @wraps(func)\n36:         async def wrapper(*args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any:\n37:             request: Request | None = None\n38:             for arg in args:\n39:                 if isinstance(arg, Request):\n40:                     request = arg\n41:                     break\n42:             if request is None:\n43:                 for _, v in kwargs.items():\n44:                     if isinstance(v, Request):\n45:                         request = v\n46:                         break\n47:             if request is None:\n48:                 raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"Request object not found\")\n49: \n50:             actor_role = request.headers.get(\"X-Actor-Role\", \"\")\n51:             level = get_trust_level(actor_role)\n52:             if level.value < minimum.value:\n53:                 raise HTTPException(\n54:                     status_code=403,\n55:                     detail=f\"Actor '{actor_role}' (trust level {level.name}) \"\n56:                            f\"does not meet minimum trust level {minimum.name}\",\n57:                 )\n58:             return await func(*args, **kwargs)\n59:         return wrapper\n60:     return decorator\n\n(End of file - total 60 lines)\n</content>"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae26635ffei03J1upu7SVTC4","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:07:37.397Z","toolInput":"{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/trust_model.py\"}","toolName":"read","toolOutput":"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/trust_model.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: from __future__ import annotations\n2: \n3: import enum\n4: from functools import wraps\n5: from typing import Any\n6: \n7: from fastapi import HTTPException, Request\n8: \n9: \n10: class TrustLevel(enum.IntEnum):\n11:     UNTRUSTED = 1\n12:     EXTERNAL_AGENT = 2\n13:     TRUSTED_AGENT = 3\n14:     OWNER = 4\n15:     SYSTEM = 5\n16: \n17: \n18: ACTOR_TRUST_MAP: dict[str, TrustLevel] = {\n19:     \"nexi\": TrustLevel.SYSTEM,\n20:     \"openclaw\": TrustLevel.OWNER,\n21:     \"claude_code\": TrustLevel.TRUSTED_AGENT,\n22:     \"opencode\": TrustLevel.TRUSTED_AGENT,\n23:     \"perception_daemon\": TrustLevel.TRUSTED_AGENT,\n24:     \"consolidation_job\": TrustLevel.TRUSTED_AGENT,\n25:     \"external\": TrustLevel.UNTRUSTED,\n26: }\n27: \n28: \n29: def get_trust_level(actor_role: str) -> TrustLevel:\n30:     return ACTOR_TRUST_MAP.get(actor_role, TrustLevel.UNTRUSTED)\n31: \n32: \n33: def requires_trust(minimum: TrustLevel):\n34:     def decorator(func: Any) -> Any:\n35:         @wraps(func)\n36:         async def wrapper(*args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any:\n37:             request: Request | None = None\n38:             for arg in args:\n39:                 if isinstance(arg, Request):\n40:                     request = arg\n41:                     break\n42:             if request is None:\n43:                 for _, v in kwargs.items():\n44:                     if isinstance(v, Request):\n45:                         request = v\n46:                         break\n47:             if request is None:\n48:                 raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"Request object not found\")\n49: \n50:             actor_role = request.headers.get(\"X-Actor-Role\", \"\")\n51:             level = get_trust_level(actor_role)\n52:             if level.value < minimum.value:\n53:                 raise HTTPException(\n54:                     status_code=403,\n55:                     detail=f\"Actor '{actor_role}' (trust level {level.name}) \"\n56:                            f\"does not meet minimum trust level {minimum.name}\",\n57:                 )\n58:             return await func(*args, **kwargs)\n59:         return wrapper\n60:     return decorator\n\n(End of file - total 60 lines)\n</content>"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8uee5_a289abafdb